/*!
    \page index.html
    \since 6.4
    \title Material Rally
    \brief Provides a qml Module Material Rally.

    Material Rally is a QML module with controls in the style of the
    \l {https://m2.material.io/design/material-studies/rally.html}{Rally Material study}. It builds
    on the Material style of Qt Quick Controls and adds controls that are made for touch and mouse
    input alike, e.g. a \l ScrollView that switches between swipe scrolling and an interactive
    scroll bar, depending on the input device used.

    \section1 Overview

    \table
    \header \li Category \li Types
    \row \li Application root
         \li \l RallyApplicationWindow, \l RallyRootPage
    \row \li Buttons and input
         \li \l Button, \l TextField, \l PasswordTextField, \l TextArea
    \row \li Containers and structure
         \li \l GroupBox, \l CollapsibleControl, \l Divider, \l ItemDelegate
    \row \li Scrolling and paging
         \li \l ScrollView, \l Flickable, \l SwipeView, \l ScrollablePage
    \row \li Dialogs and notifications
         \li \l Dialog, \l InfoDialog, \l SnackBar, \l InlineMessage
    \row \li Helpers
         \li \l BusyAction, \l Helper
    \endtable

    \section1 Getting Started

    Link your application against the \c MaterialRally CMake target and import the QML module
    into its own namespace, so the controls do not clash with the stock Qt Quick Controls of the
    same name:

    \code
    target_link_libraries(MyApp PRIVATE MaterialRally)
    \endcode

    Use \l RallyApplicationWindow (or \l RallyRootPage if the application uses QQuickView) as
    the root item. Several controls - e.g. \l Dialog, \l InfoDialog and the \l Helper functions -
    depend on it.

    \qml
    import QtQuick
    import QtQuick.Controls
    import QtQuick.Layouts
    import MaterialRally as Rally

    Rally.RallyApplicationWindow {
        width: 800
        height: 600
        title: qsTr("My Rally App")

        Rally.ScrollView {
            anchors.fill: parent

            ColumnLayout {
                width: parent.width

                Rally.GroupBox {
                    Layout.fillWidth: true
                    title: qsTr("Login")
                    infoText: qsTr("Use the credentials you got by mail.")

                    ColumnLayout {
                        anchors.fill: parent

                        Rally.TextField {
                            id: user
                            Layout.fillWidth: true
                            placeholderText: qsTr("User name")
                        }

                        Rally.PasswordTextField {
                            Layout.fillWidth: true
                            placeholderText: qsTr("Password")
                        }

                        Rally.Button {
                            text: qsTr("Login")
                            highlighted: true
                            onClicked: snackBar.pushMessage(qsTr("Welcome %1").arg(user.text))
                        }
                    }
                }
            }
        }

        Rally.SnackBar {
            id: snackBar
            anchors.bottom: parent.bottom
            anchors.horizontalCenter: parent.horizontalCenter
            inverted: true
        }
    }
    \endqml

    \section1 Reference
    \list
    \li \l{Material Rally C++ API}{C++ Classes}
    \li \l{Material Rally QML Types}{QML Types}
    \endlist
*/
